.TH SECSTORE2 1
.SH NAME
secstore2 \- Monocypher-backed secure storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B auth/secstore2
[
.BI -d " root"
] [
.BI -u " user"
] [
.BI -P " pass"
] [
.BI -N " newpass"
] [
.BI -e " epoch"
]
.BI cmd
[
.I name
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Secstore2
manages a per-user store of encrypted files.
It is a separate application from the legacy
.IR secstore (1)
service: the files are sealed locally with
Argon2id, XChaCha20-Poly1305 and BLAKE2b-256 as described in
.IR secstore2 (2),
and only ciphertext is written to the store.
The usual file is
.BR factotum ,
holding
.IR factotum (4)
keys ready to be loaded.
.PP
A store lives under
.IB root / user / name\fR.
File names are restricted to
.BR A-Za-z0-9._-
and may not begin with a dot.
The store and user directories are mode 0700 and files are mode 0600.
.PP
The commands are:
.TP
.B init
Create the store directories.
.TP
.B list
List each file with its epoch, revision, ciphertext size,
plaintext size and the first 16 bytes of the trailing BLAKE2b digest.
.TP
.BI "get " name
Decrypt
.I name
to standard output.
.TP
.BI "put " name
Encrypt standard input into
.IR name .
Every file in a store shares one password; the password is checked
against the file being replaced, or another file in the store, and the
new file reuses that file's KDF parameters, salt and epoch.
Only the first file in an empty store gets a fresh salt, and only that
first
.B put
asks for the password twice.
Replacing a file bumps its revision.
.TP
.BI "verify " name
Decrypt
.I name
and report the plaintext length.
.TP
.BI "digest " name
Print the BLAKE2b-256 digest of the whole encrypted file.
.TP
.B passwd
Decrypt every file with the old password, then re-encrypt all of them
under one new salt, increasing each epoch and revision.
Nothing is installed unless every file decrypts and seals.
.PP
The options are:
.TP
.BI -d " root"
Store root; the default is
.BR $home/lib/secstore2 .
.TP
.BI -u " user"
Store user; the default is
.BR $SC2_USER ,
or the user in
.BR /dev/user .
.TP
.BI -P " pass"
Use
.I pass
as the password instead of prompting.
.TP
.BI -N " newpass"
Use
.I newpass
as the new password for
.BR passwd .
.TP
.BI -e " epoch"
Set the epoch for
.BR put ;
it may not be lower than the existing file's.
.PP
Passwords are read from the console with echo off.
The defaults for Argon2id are
.IR t =3,
.IR m =256
MiB and one lane, which is also the floor and ceiling accepted for
.I m
(64 MiB to 256 MiB).
The emulator's default main memory pool is 32 MiB, too small for the
64 MiB floor; start
.I emu
with, for example,
.B -p main=512m
to use this store.
.SH EXAMPLES
Fetch the keys and load them:
.IP
.EX
auth/secstore2 -u glenda get factotum >/mnt/factotum/ctl
.EE
.PP
Save an edited key file:
.IP
.EX
auth/secstore2 -u glenda put factotum <factotum
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/auth/secstore2.b
.br
.B /appl/lib/secstore2.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR secstore2 (2),
.IR secstore (1),
.IR factotum (4)
.SH BUGS
The current
.I Mono
binding supports only one Argon2id lane, so files with a different
.I p
in their header are rejected.
